      "rev_n_1_165373_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_165373_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_165373",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous solution was that it didn't correctly handle the case where the chocolate price (k) could be made using a subset of the coins, but not all possible sums up to k. The new approach should focus on finding all possible sums that can be made with the subset of coins that sum to k, rather than all possible sums with the given coins.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_165373_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_f07a19aa58",
        "created_at": 1794536381.7333343
      },
      "rev_n_3_f8d183_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_f8d183_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_f8d183",
        "thought_text": "The previous approach was correct in its logic but missed handling edge cases like when the chocolate price k is 0 or when it exceeds the sum of all coins. The solution should explicitly account for these scenarios to ensure correct output.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_f8d183_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_c151f82d52",
        "created_at": 1794536412.8218012
      },
      "rev_n_2_9814c3_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_9814c3_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_9814c3",
        "thought_text": "The current approach generates all possible subsets of coins and their sums, which is inefficient and incorrect for this problem. Instead, we should use dynamic programming to find all possible sums that can be made with the given coins, and then determine which of these sums Arya can make after giving Pari a subset that sums to k. This approach will be more efficient and correct.",
